  "id": "COMPOUND:40742 - PROTEIN:6149",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Miltirone may interact with the High-affinity choline transporter through a series of target relationships. Miltirone is linked to LAMA-84, which in turn is a target of Quercitrin-7-olate and another compound, ZR-75-1. Both of these compounds are associated with the High-affinity choline transporter, indicating a potential pathway where Miltirone could influence the transporter through its interaction with LAMA-84. The scores from the paths are consistent, suggesting a plausible biological relationship, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence supports a possible role of Miltirone in modulating the activity of the choline transporter, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this interaction.",
